### TASK-260715-nzdzv3_inputs.md
> ReluxNIOSSH minimal-fork requirements

Implement a MINIMAL fork of apple/swift-nio-ssh (pinned commit 31cdc3c3391a10460dedf1170530cf651d2ca496, tag 0.14.1, Apache-2.0) as ReluxNIOSSH — a SOURCE SwiftPM dependency (ADR-019), consumed later by the NIOSSH adapter 1af33i and kept OUT of ReluxTunnelCore proper. GOAL: expose exactly the two capabilities the TASK-260715-2ny6z4 conformance contract requires that upstream keeps non-public (per TASK-260715-28ok1k audit): (1) PER-CHANNEL receive window — a public setter for the initial window on a new child channel (upstream hard-codes 1<<24 / 16 MiB internally in the window manager), plus observable remaining window and an explicit cap (contract section 9); (2) CLIENT-INITIATED REKEY by byte/time threshold — expose the internal _rekey() through a supported API (contract section 10.1). CONSTRAINTS: keep the fork MINIMAL — smallest surface changes to satisfy sections 9/10 only; do NOT rewrite the engine, do NOT alter crypto/algorithm behavior; preserve upstream Apache-2.0 license + attribution and produce a clear DELTA document listing every change vs the pin (maintainability + future rebase). Vendor at the exact pin (checksum-verify). Provide Swift Testing proving the new window setter/observer and rekey trigger actually take effect (unit-level; full functional/rekey/scale matrices are 3ikonq, gated on P0). Build + test via swift build / swift test on macOS. If exposing rekey/window minimally is infeasible without a larger change, STOP-THE-LINE with the exact delta needed — do not silently rewrite upstream internals.




