200-### Algorithms
201-
202-The pinned defaults advertise:
203-
204:- KEX: `curve25519-sha256`, `curve25519-sha256@libssh.org`, and
205-  `ecdh-sha2-nistp256/384/521`.
206-- Host/user keys: `ssh-ed25519` and ECDSA P-256/384/521.
207-- Encryption: `aes256-gcm@openssh.com` and `aes128-gcm@openssh.com`; integrity
208-  is integrated into AEAD rather than selected through a separate MAC.
209-
210-This intersects the [current OpenSSH defaults](https://man.openbsd.org/OpenBSD-current/man5/ssh_config.5),
211-but the upstream
212:[`README`](https://github.com/apple/swift-nio-ssh/blob/31cdc3c3391a10460dedf1170530cf651d2ca496/README.md)
213-explicitly describes a modern-algorithm, building-block library rather than a
214-production-ready client. RSA host/user keys, DH KEX, AES-CTR, and old MAC modes
215-are absent. That is a compatibility boundary, not a reason to weaken host-key or
216-cipher policy.
--
258-### Algorithms with the pinned backend
259-
260-OpenSSL 3.5.7 enables Ed25519, ECDSA, RSA-SHA2, AES-GCM, AES-CTR, and the current
261-ML-KEM implementations used by the selected libssh2 commit. At this source the
262:default KEX list starts with `mlkem768x25519-sha256`,
263:`mlkem768nistp256-sha256`, and `mlkem1024nistp384-sha384` when available, then
264-Curve25519, ECDH, and DH variants. The default host-key list covers Ed25519,
265-ECDSA, and RSA-SHA2, including supported OpenSSH certificate variants. Ciphers
266-include ChaCha20-Poly1305, AES-GCM, AES-CTR, and optional legacy modes.
